# Keep these out of an AI agent's context.
#
# Two reasons: privacy, and token cost. A 70 KB test log or a 640x640 JPEG read
# into context is paid for again on every subsequent turn of the session.
#
# NOTE: an ignore file is a hint that some tools honour and others do not. The
# rules that are actually ENFORCED for Claude Code live in
# .claude/settings.json under permissions.deny. Secrets are listed in both.

# --- Secrets and credentials: never read these ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
kaggle.json
hf_token*
.huggingface/
**/credentials.json
**/service-account*.json
.claude/settings.local.json

# --- Private imagery: real farm photographs, if we ever receive any ---
private/

# --- Datasets and model weights: huge, and never interesting as text ---
data/
*.onnx
*.pt
*.pth
*.parquet
*.zip
*.rar
*.tar
*.tar.gz

# --- Images and binaries ---
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.png
*.webp
*.bmp
*.tiff
*.pdf

# --- Build and dependency trees ---
.venv/
**/.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
node_modules/
dist/
build/
.next/
android/
ios/

# --- Logs, scratch, lockfiles ---
*.log
*.part
.superpowers/
package-lock.json
yarn.lock
pnpm-lock.yaml
uv.lock
